# OpenTUI iOS port patch -- 0001
# Title: add aarch64-ios (iPhoneOS) library target + iPhoneOS SDK framework wiring
# Upstream: anomalyco/opentui @ v0.8.0 (commit 738067f47e940dcec3f5aab74868908574335c6c)
# Files: packages/native/build.zig, packages/native/src/clipboard/host.zig,
#        packages/native/src/miniaudio_shim_ios.m (new)
# Why: OpenTUI v0.8.0 ships native libraries for linux/macos/windows only. The port needs an
#      iPhoneOS arm64 libopentui.dylib that the Node 26 iOS runtime can load via node:ffi
#      (Phase C/D). This patch adds the target and the Apple-SDK plumbing:
#      - SUPPORTED_TARGETS gains aarch64-ios.15.0 (output_name aarch64-ios); the custom-target
#        fallback already accepted arbitrary Zig target strings.
#      - new -Dios-sdk=... / IOS_SDK_PATH resolution (iPhoneOS*.sdk with CoreFoundation/ImageIO/
#        CoreAudio/AudioToolbox); buildTarget refuses iOS targets without it with a clear message.
#      - .ios arms for the miniaudio/image/libwebp C flags (-isysroot <iPhoneOS.sdk>). On iOS the
#        miniaudio CoreAudio backend includes <AVFoundation/AVFoundation.h> and uses Objective-C
#        (AVAudioSession), so the iOS target compiles src/miniaudio_shim_ios.m (an Objective-C
#        translation unit including miniaudio_shim.c); other targets compile the C shim directly.
#      - iPhoneOS framework linking: CoreFoundation, CoreAudio, AudioToolbox, Foundation,
#        AVFoundation (no AppKit/UIKit), plus the SDK usr/lib library search path so the linker
#        finds the SDK libSystem stub. No global `zig build --sysroot` is passed: it is global to
#        every compilation unit (including host tools and Zig`s bundled libc++ sub-build) and
#        broke both. Explicit -isysroot flags are only given to the C/Objective-C shims.
#      - C++ (yoga) stays hermetic: Zig`s bundled libc++ and Darwin libc headers are built
#        together for the target. Mixing them with the iPhoneOS SDK libc++ headers does not
#        compile (SDK libc++ expects C23 ::nullptr_t from SDK C headers while Zig supplies its
#        own libc headers).
#      - translate-c steps (miniaudio.h, yoga-bridge.h, opentui.h) get explicit iPhoneOS SDK
#        include and framework search paths (translate-c does not use the target sysroot).
#      - new -Duucode-tables=<path> option: the iOS build passes a pre-generated uucode tables.zig
#        (vendored in patches/opentui-ios/files/uucode-tables.zig.gz, generated once with Zig 0.16.0)
#        so the build skips the native uucode_generate host executable entirely (no host tools in
#        the iOS build graph).
#      - clipboard: iPhoneOS keeps the "unsupported" clipboard path (the macOS implementation is
#        the AppKit NSPasteboard shim, which does not exist on iOS); the worker-thread compile
#        switch gains an .ios arm.
#      - ghostty VT stays disabled for iOS (existing availability check: non-linux/macos/windows).
# Test: zig build -Dlibrary-target=aarch64-ios.15.0 -Doptimize=ReleaseFast -Dios-sdk=$IOS_SDK
#       -Duucode-tables=uucode-tables.zig from packages/native on macos-15 with Zig 0.16.0;
#       scripts/build-opentui-ios.sh extracts the tables and runs build + static validation.
#       Status: build feasibility only -- NOT device-verified; loading via node:ffi is Phase D.

